## The kit (browserscale-kit)

The harness already wired config + store + logging. Reach for these helpers
instead of hand-rolling; the kit *helps*, it doesn't dictate.

Import paths: `github.com/browserscale/browserscale-kit/{form,store,input,proxy,mail,logger,module}`.
Every field referenced in a `Schema()` snippet below must also exist on your
`Config` struct — add it there first.

**Config — `form`** (in `module.go`): typed, fluent, bound to your `Config`
struct; edited in the TUI and saved as JSON.

```go
f.String("cloudKey", &m.cfg.CloudKey).Label("API key").Required()
f.Int("threads", &m.cfg.Threads).Default(1).Min(1).Max(64)
f.Bool("headless", &m.cfg.Headless).Default(true)
f.Select("region", &m.cfg.Region).Option("us", "US").Option("de", "Germany")
f.File("proxies", &m.cfg.Proxies).Tag(form.TagProxies)          // validated file picker
f.StringList("countries", &m.cfg.Countries)
// conditional: only show when another field is set
f.File("proxies", &m.cfg.Proxies).ShowWhenTruthy("useProxies")
```

**State — `store`** (`env.Store`): SQLite KV for idempotent re-runs / resume.
Namespace per module; wrap structs with `NewJSON[T]`.

```go
ns := env.Store.Namespace(m.Name())
seen := store.NewJSON[Record](ns)
rec, ok, _ := seen.Get(key)                 // skip if already done
seen.Put(key, Record{Status: "done"})       // mark done; survives restarts
```

**Input — `input`**: error-honest list loading + a thread-safe consumer.

```go
q, _ := input.LineQueue(filepath.Join(env.FilesDirectory, "emails.txt"))  // *Queue[string]
for {
    item, ok := q.Next()                     // one item per worker, drains
    if !ok { break }
}
rows, _ := input.CSV(path)                   // [][]string, RFC-4180 (header is yours to skip)
rows, _ := input.Columns(path, ":")          // [][]string — you decide the meaning
q2 := input.NewQueue(records)                // *Queue[T] from any typed slice (e.g. []account)
line, _ := q.Random()                        // sample with replacement (proxies/names)
```

Typical CSV → typed queue (this is what the generated `queue` `run.go` does):

```go
rows, _ := input.CSV(filepath.Join(env.FilesDirectory, m.cfg.InputFile))
var accs []account
for i, r := range rows {
    if len(r) < 2 || (i == 0 && strings.EqualFold(r[0], "email")) { continue }
    accs = append(accs, account{email: r[0], password: r[1]})
}
q := input.NewQueue(accs)                     // *Queue[account]
```

Validate CSV shape in the configurator (caught *before* the run starts):

```go
f.File("inputFile", &m.cfg.InputFile).Tag(form.TagLines).
    ValidateFile(func(path string) error {
        rows, err := input.CSV(path)
        if err != nil { return err }
        if len(rows) == 0 { return errors.New("empty csv") }
        return nil
    }).Required()
```

**Proxies — `proxy`**: parse the usual formats + a rotating pool.

```go
pool, _ := proxy.LoadPool(filepath.Join(env.FilesDirectory, "proxies.txt"))
p, ok := pool.Next()                          // round-robin; also pool.Random()
// p.Host, p.Port, p.Username, p.Password, p.URL()
```

**Email codes — `mail`**: a persistent IMAP `CodeFetcher` for OTP / verification
emails. Open one per mailbox at start; call `FetchCode` from workers (it
multiplexes over one kept-alive, auto-reconnecting connection).

```go
f, _ := mail.NewCodeFetcher(host, port, user, pass)   // once, in Init
defer f.Stop()
// CRITICAL: capture the timestamp BEFORE the action that triggers the send,
// then pass it (minus a ~60s clock-skew buffer) as `since`, so you match the
// FRESH code and never a stale one left in a reused / catch-all mailbox.
mailTime := time.Now().UnixMilli()
browser.Click(ctx, browserscale.CSS("#send-code"))    // triggers the email
code, _ := f.FetchCode(ctx, from, toEmail, "", `(\d{6})`, mailTime-60_000, 60_000, true)
// args: from, to, subjectKeyword, codeRegex(1 group), sinceUnixMilli, timeoutMs, deleteAfterFetch
```

IMAP `SINCE` is day-granular, so `FetchCode` filters on millisecond
INTERNALDATE itself — that's why the `mailTime` handshake matters. Full detail
in the `mail` package doc (`go doc github.com/browserscale/browserscale-kit/mail.CodeFetcher`).

**Logging — `logger`** (`env.Logger`): `logger.NewLogger("[tag]", env.Logger)`
gives a scoped child; `.Println / .Success / .Error`.

**Output — `env.Output(file, line, mode)`**: append/write result files under
the task folder (`mode` = `"append"` or `"write"`).

